      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Doorstep Delivery Handover, Inventory Verification &amp; Placement at Koderma</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>The final phase of the logistics operation at Koderma demands rigorous attention to detail to ensure asset integrity and site readiness. The process begins with daylight delivery verification, a critical step where the incoming consignment is meticulously cross-referenced against the original inventory bilty.</p>
<p>This daylight inspection ensures that all crates and pallets are accounted for, free from transit damage, and match the documented quantities exactly. Any discrepancies must be flagged immediately for rectification before the uncrating process commences, preserving the chain of custody and accountability throughout the supply chain.</p>
<p>Once the inventory is verified, personnel proceed to the uncrating and testing phase. Electrical and mechanical items require specialized handling; upon removal from their protective packaging, these units undergo immediate functional testing.</p>
<p>Technicians verify power connections, check for mechanical integrity, and run diagnostic sequences to confirm that all components operate within specified parameters. This pre-installation testing is vital to identify potential defects early, minimizing downtime and ensuring that all equipment is fully operational before it is integrated into the main facility infrastructure.</p>
<p>Simultaneously, the clean furniture placement protocol is executed with precision. Furniture items, which have been carefully packed to withstand transit, are moved to their designated locations within the facility. The placement must adhere to the pre-planned layout diagrams, ensuring optimal workflow and aesthetic consistency.</p>
<p>Each piece is checked for surface damage or scratches, and any minor imperfections are documented. The arrangement is finalized to create a professional and functional environment, ready for immediate use by the staff and operations team.</p>
<p>Finally, the swift removal of packing debris is essential to maintain site hygiene and safety. All cardboard, foam, plastic wrapping, and other packaging materials are collected and disposed of according to local environmental regulations. This rapid cleanup prevents clutter, reduces slip hazards, and ensures that the Koderma site remains orderly and compliant with safety standards.</p>
<p>By adhering to this structured protocol, the team ensures a seamless transition from transit to operation, maximizing efficiency and maintaining the high standards expected of the Koderma facility. This comprehensive approach not only protects the valuable assets but also fosters a safe and productive working environment from the moment the delivery trucks arrive.</p>
